      "problem": "A sandwich costs $$12$ before tax. If a $9.5%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total price after tax?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the total price after tax, we apply a $9.5%$ increase to the original cost.\n\nIncreasing by $9.5%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+9.5%=109.5%=1.095\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.095:$\n\n$$\n12\\times 1.095=13.14.\n$$\n\nSo, the total price after tax is $$13.14.$",
